meta {
  name: Add Calendar Days
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/calendar/days
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{hrAdminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "source": "manual",
    "days": [
      {
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "kind": "closure",
        "label": "Office closed — flooding",
        "reason": "Burst pipe overnight; office unusable."
      }
    ]
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("hrCalendarDayId", res.getBody().days[0].id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("echoes the row with its author", function () {
    const day = res.getBody().days[0];
    expect(day.date).to.equal("2026-11-03");
    expect(day.kind).to.equal("closure");
    expect(day.source).to.equal("manual");
    expect(day.reason).to.be.a("string");
    expect(day.createdBy).to.have.property("name");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /hr/calendar/days — add holidays, closures, special working days (PAC-161)

  - **Module:** `hr` · **Permission:** `agency:hr:admin`

  ## Body
  ```json
  { "source": "import" | "manual" | "onboarding",
    "days": [{ "date": "YYYY-MM-DD", "kind": "holiday" | "closure" | "special_working_day",
               "label": "…", "reason": "…" }] }
  ```
  A `manual` batch needs a `reason` on every row (the audit trail for a hand
  change); `import` / `onboarding` rows carry none. 1–400 rows.

  ## Semantics
  - One **active** row per date. A date already on the calendar is a `409`
    naming every clashing date, and **nothing from the batch is written**.
  - Duplicate dates inside one batch are a `400`.
  - A `special_working_day` opens the office on a weekend or holiday; a
    `holiday` / `closure` closes it whatever the workweek says.
  - `createdBy` is stamped from the request (the authorship plugin).

  ## Response `201` — `{ "days": [AgencyCalendarDayView…] }`, sorted by date.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — validation. `409` — date already active. `403` — not an HR admin.
}
